      "letterAudio": "audio/sv/letters/sv-o.mp3",
      "memoryTrick": "Tricky! Swedish 'o' can sound like English 'oo' in 'moon' (as in 'bo' — to live) or like 'aw' in 'law' (as in 'ost' — cheese). Context and region affect which you'll hear. When in doubt, round your lips tightly.",
