      "letterAudio": "audio/sv/letters/sv-u.mp3",
      "memoryTrick": "A sound English doesn't have! Round your lips tightly as if saying 'oo', but keep your tongue forward as if saying 'ee'. The result is a compressed, buzzy vowel — somewhere between 'ew' and a whistle.",
